**Journal:** *Bioresources and Bioprocessing* (2026)

**DOI:** https://doi.org/10.1186/s40643-026-01126-0

This work presents the metabolic engineering of *Thermothelomyces heterothallica* for cellobionate production using CRISPR-Cas9-mediated genome editing. The engineered TH11 strain produced 64 mM cellobionate within five days and achieved approximately 88% cellulose conversion from alkali-pretreated wheat straw without the addition of external cellulases, demonstrating the potential of fungal metabolic engineering for sustainable biomanufacturing of value-added bioproducts.
